    {
      "id": "much-ado-about-nothing/sceneIV_25.2/p@128405",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "DOGBERRY.\nDost thou not suspect my place? Dost thou not suspect my years? O that he were here to write me down an ass! but, masters, remember that I am an ass; though it be not written down, yet forget not that I am an ass. No, thou villain, thou art full of piety, as shall be proved upon thee by good witness. I am a wise fellow; and, which is more, an officer; and, which is more, a householder; and, which is more, as pretty a piece of flesh as any in Messina; and one that knows the law, go to; and a rich fellow enough, go to; and a fellow that hath had losses; and one that hath two gowns, and everything handsome about him. Bring him away. O that I had been writ down an ass!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
